package wasmcloud:nats-jetstream-replay;

/// Order processing over JetStream, with replay.
///
/// The host pushes each new delivery into `jetstream-handler`, which is the
/// at-least-once path. The handler is per-request: it holds no consumer and no
/// stream, so it scales down to nothing between bursts.
///
/// `js-processor` carries the whole `wasmcloud:nats` import surface, which is
/// what makes this one line: the grant, not the import list, is what bounds
/// reach, and imports the component never calls are dropped at build time.
/// `jetstream` is what this one uses, for the durable publish and for `scan` —
/// a replay from an arbitrary stream sequence without creating a consumer, the
/// thing `wasmcloud:messaging` cannot express.
world nats-jetstream-replay {
  include wasmcloud:nats/js-processor@0.1.0;
}
